{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>If</b> — the poet's words: \"If I said in my heart,\" or [if] I say to others." "<b>I would tell</b> — like אלה, and the word אלה is missing, as in ה' הטוב יכפר בעד אותם שאכלו הפסח, for it is not written כי כל לבבו שב אל חזקיהו אהיה בוגד בדור בניך, HaShem — that the faith of the heart not be in their faith. And behold, a bet may be missing: behold, \"in the generation of your children\" — they are those from whom I received the Torah."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {1 "The comment is textually difficult: the biblical phrases cited (from 2 Chron 30 and 29) are stitched together in a way that resists fluent rendering, and the logical flow between the missing-אלה argument, the citation, and the remark about בדור בניך is opaque in the source; translated hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:16.450150657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}